---
import Site from '../components/Site.astro';
import {projects} from '../lib/projects';
const questions = ['How can an inspection system distinguish a genuine fault from sensor uncertainty, and verify an authorized action safely?','How should evidence, cultural context, and human approval move between research, creative work, and campaign analysis?','How can stories and quizzes preserve source accuracy while supporting accessible, curriculum-aligned revision?','Which storage measurements and records make an alert useful without treating it as proof that food is safe?','What guidance, material compatibility, targeting, and retrieval requirements must be evaluated before laboratory testing?','How should sensor reliability, privacy, trend interpretation, and human medical oversight shape astronaut health monitoring?'];
---
<Site title="Our Journey | Verified Scornis Project Updates" description="Follow genuine Scornis research progress, simulation milestones, prototype experiments, technical learning, and collaboration announcements as they are documented."><div class="wrap"><section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Research / Reflection / Progress</p><h1>Our Journey.</h1><p>Research progress, simulation milestones, prototype experiments, competition participation, technical learning, collaboration announcements, demonstrations, and product updates—documented only when verified.</p></section><section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Concept documentation</p><h2>Six concepts. Six research priorities.</h2><p>These editorial notes document the project briefs supplied by Scornis, not experiments, demonstrations, or completed milestones.</p><div class="grid">{projects.map((p,i)=><article class="card"><div class="card-body"><p class="eyebrow">{p.name}</p><h3>{p.name}: defining the research direction</h3><p>{p.description}</p><h4>Documented scope</h4><p>{p.status} Founded by {p.founder}. The brief identifies {p.features.slice(0,3).join(', ').toLowerCase()} as research directions, not verified operational capabilities.</p><h4>Research question</h4><p>{questions[i]}</p><h4>What the brief establishes</h4><p>{p.note}</p><h4>Next steps</h4><p>{p.roadmap.slice(0,2).join(' → ')}</p><a class="project-link" href={`/projects/${p.slug}`}>View Project ↗</a></div></article>)}</div></section><section class="cta"><h2>Contribute a technical perspective.</h2><p>Discuss research questions, testing approaches, or opportunities for responsible collaboration with Scornis.</p><a class="button primary" href="/contact">Contact Scornis ↗</a></section></div></Site>